ence  and then go on to  to go to law school and kind of spend a  lot of time really in that race uh  chasing the things that people chase in  those sorts of circles uh and and  honestly long story short once once  covey hit and had a chance to really  kind of sit down and evaluate my life  you know and being in dc you really  think that that machine needs you to run  uh and everyone thinks so so much of  themselves but i really began to realize  that  that  my heart was really very much empty  because i wasn't able to give back uh in  the way that i really want to i saw in  the media how chicago was really being  portrayed uh people were drawn to me  because i was from chicago but not  necessarily because of me but because of  the things that they saw and they  associated  with chicago the things that the media  had associated  with chicago and it was just really  really important to me to not waste  another day uh of my life and of my  of my gifts that that i have uh as well  so i after cover was over i came back in  market to start to volunteer here i  really felt like there was no better  place for me to be uh and to have  immediate impact uh rather than here at  project food and i  the rest is pretty much  history you know what i want to say  something because here's a success story  here's a young man who's been with us  since he was 12. how old are you now 35  so he's 35 now so here's a young man  who's been with us for a long time  and  you grew up in the hood  not only did you grow up in the hood but  you  went to school  educated yourself got a law degree  and  you worked in dc  but realized it wasn't fulfilling  and  being involved in government isn't  always the most fulfilling thing  yeah and you decided to come back and  work in the hood  why is why work  why come back and work in the hood why  is that so important yeah because  exposure is really everything man i  if we're not for the individuals who are  in my life that that were in the church  and just hanging up hanging around i  they really enabled me to really see  that there was more out there for myself  and more more in  in me as well i and i really do believe  that you can't be what you can't see so  it's important for for me to yeah to  come back and really like just be the  best version of myself that i could  possibly be because i know there are so  many young people who are watching uh so  many folks so many ways in which that we  get to  to interact and affect and positively  affect the lives of those who are in  this community uh as well and honestly  just to come back and just love on my  community right to be an example of  someone coming back to where they're  from and not leaving where they're from  and investing and then sticking with it  in order to see it become what you know  that it can be and be  and really help to deliver a life and a  community that that these residents  really do truly deserve  you know what and that's what it's going  to take  it's going to take some people coming  back home  to the community  it's going to take people  who have achieved educationally maybe  professionally who make a conscious  decision to say you know what  the hood needs me  my neighborhood needs me there are some  young boys that need positive mentors  and so we want to encourage all of you  who are educated and professional  man please come back home help us in  this endeavor to transform a  neighborhood because that's what it's  really all about brian thank you for  being part of project hood and helping  to run our organization thank you for  being back and thank you for being a  positive example thank you so much for  having me i appreciate it thank you all  for joining rooftop revelations and  until tomorrow  peace  you

